        "time_seconds": 25.595904111862183,
        "error": null,
        "agent_output": "Done! The bug was on line 171. The condition `while pos > tic_len:` is logically impossible (pos starts at 0 and tic_len is always >= 0), so the backtick pairing loop never executes. This means pipes inside inline code blocks are never filtered out and incorrectly treated as table delimiters.\n\nChanging it to `while pos < tic_len:` fixes the logic so that:\n1. Matching backtick pairs are identified\n2. Regions containing code blocks are stored\n3. Pipes within those regions are filtered out\n4. Only actual table delimiters are used to split rows\n\nThe fix is minimal and corrects the logic error that was preventing inline code blocks (with pipes inside) from being properly handled in table cells.\n",
        "rate_limited": false
      }
